      "budget_share": 0.5,
      "why": "Pipelined is the only family that guarantees 1 result/cycle throughput. To meet 400 MSPS, Fmax must be >= 400 MHz. On Artix-7, a fully pipelined CORDIC with moderate width (14-16) and moderate iterations (12-16) is the most likely candidate to hit 400+ MHz while keeping LUTs low. Accuracy constraint (<= 2^-12) requires sufficient n_iter and data_width; 14-16 bits with 12-16 iterations should comfortably exceed 12-bit accuracy."
    },
